<title>SINGAPORE: Wah Shing 1996 net profit up 19 percent.</title>
<headline>Wah Shing 1996 net profit up 19 percent.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			    102.77 vs 127.52</p>
<p>    Dividend (HK cents)		   7.50 vs   nil</p>
<p>    Group shr (HK cents)		 27.00 vs  38.00</p>
<p>    Turnover			    1,015.89 vs 905.64</p>
<p>    Interest income			 2.44 vs   6.52</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		    0.76 vs   1.88</p>
<p>    Depreciation (expense)	     24.48 vs  19.61</p>
<p>    Profits from associates	     2.30 vs   1.21</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			104.15 vs 124.17</p>
<p>    Tax					(1.70)vs   3.41</p>
<p>    Minorities				0.32 vs  (0.06)</p>
<p>    Dividend pay date:		    May 17,1997</p>
<p>    Last day books open:		  May 07, 1997</p>
<p>Note - Wah Shing International is a manufacturer of toys.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703088)</p>
